<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Easter Ross</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/easter">Easter</a> Ross is the eastern lowland part of Ross in the northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scottish-highlands">Scottish Highlands</a>, between the Cromarty and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dornoch-firth">Dornoch Firths</a>. Ptolemy placed the Decantae there. It is rich in Pictish carved stones and has an early monastery at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portmahomack">Portmahomack</a>, and many historians now place the Pictish kingdom of Fortriu around Moray and Easter Ross.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/easter-ross.jpg" alt="Easter Ross" width="320" height="314" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Grinner · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ScotlandEasterRossWesterRoss.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>A 2023 study of eight whole genomes from Lundin Links in Fife and Balintore in <b>Easter Ross</b> found broad affinities with Iron Age Britons and present-day people of western Scotland, Wales, Northern Ireland and Northumbria, supporting a local origin.</blockquote><a href="/culture/picts">Picts · Origins</a></li><li><blockquote>Ptolemy's Geography of about 150 places the Decantae on the east coast of the northern Highlands, usually located in <b>Easter Ross</b> and the Black Isle around the Cromarty and Dornoch Firths.</blockquote><a href="/state/decantae">Decantae</a></li><li><blockquote>Long located in Strathearn, it is now usually placed around Moray and <b>Easter Ross</b>, following work by Alex Woolf.</blockquote><a href="/state/kingdom-of-fortriu">Kingdom of Fortriu</a></li></ul></section>
